SECTION E: REPRESENTATION HEALTH (embedding std / effective rank)
============================================================
D10: no representation-health statistic is logged anywhere in the training
or eval pipeline, so a fully collapsed representation (z -> constant) would
present as an excellent, high-similarity result in every test above. This
is the single cheapest measurement the debate names as decisive (Sec 4.3,
item 3) -- it distinguishes 'accurate predictions' from 'everything looks
similar because the embedding space has collapsed'. Full width = 256 dims.

